{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>In the thickness of the cloud.</b> Even though all the prophecies of Moses from the time of the giving of the Torah onward were in the luminous mirror, as it says: וּתְמֻנַת ה' יַבִּיט (Numbers 12:8), nevertheless this prophecy of his was in the thickness of the cloud." "<b>So that the people may hear.</b> And also in you they shall believe forever. They shall believe in the possibility of your prophecy being face to face — for I shall indeed speak with them face to face, without any dream, as it says: פָּנִים בְּפָנִים דִּבֶּר ה' עִמָּכֶם (Deuteronomy 5:4) — which means that a man prophesies while still making use of his senses, and this they considered impossible. Now they will also believe in you, that your prophecy will be in this manner, as it says: וְדִבֶּר ה' אֶל מֹשֶׁה פָּנִים אֶל פָּנִים (Exodus 33:11). Therefore they said: הַיּוֹם הַזֶּה רָאִינוּ כִּי יְדַבֵּר אֱלֹהִים אֶת הָאָדָם וָחָי (Deuteronomy 5:21). For indeed they had no doubt about the possibility of prophecy, and they knew that the Patriarchs and Moses and Aaron and Miriam had already prophesied. But the prophecy of no prophet until now had been except in vision and dream, as He, blessed be He, explained in saying: בְּמַרְאָה אֵלָיו אֶתְוַדָּע, בַּחֲלוֹם אֲדַבֶּר בּוֹ (Numbers 12:6). But regarding Moses' prophecy while still making use of his senses, they had doubt — had they themselves not also prophesied in this manner until now. And through this they shall believe in the words of Moses, and no prophet will be able to arise against them, for their prophecy will not be at this level." "<b>And Moses reported the words of the people to YHWH.</b> When he heard the arrangement of his Maker, so that they would believe in the kind of prophecy he had, he perceived the people's doubt and reported their words — for he thought that the reason they said כֹּל אֲשֶׁר דִּבֶּר ה' נַעֲשֶׂה, and did not say merely כֵּן נַעֲשֶׂה, was because they were uncertain whether Moses' prophecy of this kind was the direct word of YHWH or came through an angel — and that perhaps if they accepted upon themselves the words of an angel, he would scrutinize them as by a hair's breadth and would not forgive, as it says (Exodus 23:21): כִּי לֹא יִשָּׂא לְפִשְׁעֲכֶם. And so they said that they would do nothing other than the word of YHWH alone."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:26:21.938170896Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}